  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/orthospinus_franciscensis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Orthospinus franciscensis is a tetra endemic to the Rio Sao Francisco in Brazil. It reaches only 8 cm maximum length.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/orthospinus_franciscensis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Endemic to the Rio Sao Francisco in Brazil.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/orthospinus_franciscensis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Keeping and also probably breeding is the same as in the Silver Dollar (Brachychalcinus orbicularis). However, O. franciscensis stays smaller, reaching only 8 cm maximum length.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/orthospinus_franciscensis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Lexicon: Orthospinus means \"erected spine\", which refers to a spine placed before the dorsal fin. franciscensis refers to the origin of the species, the Rio Sao Francisco.</p><p>This species was imported for the first time.</p>"
    }
